.TH "WEBTRANSPORTSENDSTREAM.SENDGROUP" "3JS" "September 1, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
WebTransportSendStream.sendGroup \- WebTransportSendStream: sendGroup
property
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]sendGroup\f[B]\f[R] property of the
\f[CR]WebTransportSendStream\f[R] interface represents the
\f[CR]WebTransportSendGroup\f[R] that this stream is grouped under for
the purposes of \f[CR]sendOrder\f[R] prioritization.
.PP
Within a group, bytes queued for sending on streams and datagrams with a
higher \f[CR]sendOrder\f[R] are sent before any bytes from
lower\-priority ones.
Different groups are expected to be treated as equals for the purposes
of bandwidth allocation \(em though the precise way bandwidth is divided
between groups is implementation\-defined.
.SH VALUE
A \f[CR]WebTransportSendGroup\f[R] object, or \f[CR]null\f[R] to specify
the default send group.
The default value is \f[CR]null\f[R].
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]InvalidStateError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if set to a \f[CR]WebTransportSendGroup\f[R] that is associated
with a different \f[CR]WebTransport\f[R] object than this stream.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
The example below creates a send group using the
\f[CR]WebTransport.createSendGroup()\f[R] method, and then uses it with
a \f[CR]sendOrder\f[R] value, to prioritize the stream relative to other
streams and datagrams that are part of the same group:
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] sendGroup = transport.createSendGroup();

\f[B]const\f[R] stream = \f[B]await\f[R] transport.createUnidirectionalStream({
  sendGroup,
  sendOrder: 1,
});

console.log(stream.sendGroup === sendGroup); \f[I]// true\f[R]
.EE
